@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Roll back one unit to an earlier commit (L2-086)
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
actor "Owner" as owner
participant "Deploy marketing / Deploy app" as deploy
box "Azure VM /opt/sycapooke" #D1FADF
  participant ".env" as env
  participant "docker compose" as compose
end box
alt through GitHub
  owner -> deploy : Run workflow (the unit to roll back), ref = older full SHA
  deploy -> deploy : checkout ref; build and push that unit's images tagged ref
  deploy -> compose : MARKETING_TAG=ref or APP_TAG=ref; pull; migrator (app only, no-op); up -d --no-deps <own services>
  deploy --> owner : smoke test passes; the other unit is unchanged
else on the VM
  owner -> env : set MARKETING_TAG=<older sha> or APP_TAG=<older sha>
  owner -> compose : docker compose up -d --no-deps marketing (or api worker app)
  compose --> owner : that unit runs the older images
end
note over owner, compose : Migrations are forward-only: going back past a breaking schema change needs a compatible migration first.
@enduml
